# Tests from nvm's own suite (tests/reference/nvm-v0.40.8/test) that are not
# run as parity cases, as `<reason>: <path under test/>`. A path ending in `/`
# covers a whole directory. Reasons:
#
#   installer      tests nvm's install.sh, which nvmimic does not ship
#   fixture        an executable file the tests use, not a test itself
#   docker         only meaningful inside nvm's Ubuntu 16.04 test image
#   mock-internal  redefines one of nvm's internal functions as a shell
#                  function and expects nvm to call it, which a program
#                  outside the shell cannot do
#   mock-tool      redefines an outside program (clang, wget) as a shell
#                  function or alias and expects nvm to run that instead
#   hook-function  names a shell function as NVM_INSTALL_THIRD_PARTY_HOOK,
#                  which a program outside the shell cannot call
#   network        needs the real internet or Docker
#   real-node      installs real Node releases from nodejs.org (0.8 to 9.x and
#                  io.js, some built from source), which the offline test
#                  mirror does not hold. `cargo xtask parity --network` runs
#                  these and nothing else
#
# A line that names one test wins over a line that names its directory, so
# the six tests under the real-node directories that also redefine one of
# nvm's functions are listed below as mock-internal and stay out of the
# network pass too.
installer: install_script/
fixture: mocks/
fixture: fixtures/
docker: xenial/
real-node: slow/
real-node: sourcing/
real-node: installation_node/
real-node: installation_iojs/
